0..77 Comment "// A group\'s laws stated as rules, the coincidence check certifying each with"
78..156 Comment "// the others: the structure the circle\'s loops carry under composition, whose"
157..226 Comment "// laws `circle-group.gandr` proves as paths. The unit on both sides,"
227..301 Comment "// associativity and the inverse\'s own two laws join among themselves; the"
302..377 Comment "// cancellation `mul(inv(x), x) ==> e()` does not until completion adds the"
378..451 Comment "// cells it derives (Knuth and Bendix, _Simple Word Problems in Universal"
452..496 Comment "// Algebras_, 1970, § 7), and is refused in"
497..554 Comment "// `../../pathological/identity/group-inverse-law.gandr`."
556..633 Comment "/// A group\'s unit, associativity and inverse laws, each a rule: `e()` is the"
634..687 Comment "/// unit and `a()`, `b()` two elements the rows read."
688..690 Other "@["
691..701 Other "normalizes"
701..702 Other "("
702..703 StringLit "\""
703..751 StringLit "mul(mul(e, inv(inv(a))), mul(b, e)) ~> mul(a, b)"
